{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ולא יאכל", :translit "v'lo yei'acheil", :gloss "and it shall not be eaten"} {:he "ולא הנאה", :translit "v'lo hana'ah", :gloss "and no benefit"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "ולא יאכל", :b "ולא הנאה"}], :frame {:text "The ox that killed a person is stoned and its flesh may not be eaten (Exodus 21:28). The verse literally prohibits eating the flesh, which by Torah law is not a standard nevelah prohibition since the animal was alive when sentenced. The gematria teaching that 'no benefit' (ולא הנאה) equals 'it shall not be eaten' (ולא יאכל) signals that the prohibition extends beyond consumption to any use or benefit derived from the condemned animal.", :sources ["Exodus 21:28" "Mishnah Sanhedrin 54a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "ולא יאכל", :a-value 98, :b "ולא הנאה", :b-value 98, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:18:09.603308100Z", :model "glm-5.2"}